WEBVTT

00:33.952 --> 00:36.203
♪ Hey ♪

00:36.204 --> 00:37.956
♪ Here she comes now ♪

00:40.751 --> 00:42.668
♪ Oh, you know her ♪

00:42.669 --> 00:45.170
♪ Would you look at that hair ♪

00:45.171 --> 00:47.381
♪ Yeah, you know her ♪

00:47.382 --> 00:49.049
♪ Check out those shoes ♪

00:49.050 --> 00:51.010
♪ She looks like
She stepped out of ♪

00:51.011 --> 00:53.972
♪ The middle
Of somebody's blues ♪

00:56.600 --> 00:58.183
♪ She looks like
The Sunday comics ♪

00:58.184 --> 00:59.352
Linda.

01:00.103 --> 01:01.353
♪ She thinks she's-- ♪

01:01.354 --> 01:02.814
Earth to Linda.

01:04.941 --> 01:06.317
Oh.

01:08.194 --> 01:09.612
Still working
on the company report?

01:09.613 --> 01:11.906
Uh, I finished that last week.

01:11.907 --> 01:14.784
I was just working on
some projections for next month.

01:14.785 --> 01:15.951
You include
last year's numbers?

01:15.952 --> 01:17.244
Mm-hmm.
All index-correlated

01:17.245 --> 01:19.998
with next year's
estimated quarterlies included.

01:20.498 --> 01:23.208
- You're amazing.
- Oh.

01:23.209 --> 01:25.086
God, I have so much trouble
with this stuff.

01:25.587 --> 01:27.547
All right. They're all waiting.

01:27.548 --> 01:30.299
Showtime. I'm right behind ya.

01:30.300 --> 01:31.884
- Oh.
- Oh.

01:31.885 --> 01:33.804
No, they shrunk it down
to a smaller group.

01:34.262 --> 01:36.472
I'm actually just,
uh, dropping it off.

01:39.935 --> 01:42.269
I-I put the numbers together.

01:42.270 --> 01:43.729
They told me they wanted me
in the room

01:43.730 --> 01:45.064
in case there were
any questions.

01:45.065 --> 01:47.192
Questions.
Yeah, I don't really know.

01:47.859 --> 01:50.611
I mean, you know how it's been
around here lately, Linda,

01:50.612 --> 01:51.613
it's just all...

01:52.197 --> 01:53.406
...up in the air.

01:55.366 --> 01:56.200
Yeah.

01:56.201 --> 01:58.661
But don't worry. They'll know
who did the heavy lifting.

01:58.662 --> 02:01.247
Your name is right on top.

02:03.959 --> 02:04.835
Okay.

02:05.501 --> 02:07.003
- Okay.
- Thanks.

02:07.629 --> 02:08.797
Good luck in there.

02:12.092 --> 02:13.093
Well...

02:13.594 --> 02:15.970
Guess that old
elevator to success

02:15.971 --> 02:17.931
is out of order again, huh?

02:18.974 --> 02:20.808
- What?
- Oh.

02:20.809 --> 02:23.979
I was just saying, we're gonna
have to keep taking the stairs.

02:24.520 --> 02:26.522
One step at a time.

02:28.108 --> 02:29.108
Oi!

02:29.109 --> 02:31.612
- Chase!
- Oh. Hey, what's up?

02:31.945 --> 02:33.320
- 'Sup?
- Uh...

02:33.321 --> 02:35.906
A few of us after work
are hitting Milly and Al's for--

02:35.907 --> 02:36.949
- So down.
- Oh!

02:36.950 --> 02:40.953
Milly and--
That's the best karaoke in town.

02:40.954 --> 02:42.580
- Yeah, it is.
- Could really go for a song

02:42.581 --> 02:44.123
and a drink tonight.

02:44.124 --> 02:47.628
My go-to is
"One Way Or Another."

02:49.004 --> 02:49.879
Uh...

02:49.880 --> 02:50.796
- Is that...
- No?

02:50.797 --> 02:52.256
- No.
- Blondie?

02:52.257 --> 02:54.091
- Debbie Harry? Oh, man.
- No.

02:54.092 --> 02:55.175
- All right.
- All right.

02:55.176 --> 02:56.844
"I'm gonna get ya, get ya,
get ya, get ya."

02:56.845 --> 02:57.845
Hey!

02:57.846 --> 02:59.472
You gotta Google her.

02:59.723 --> 03:01.725
Um, do you have a go-to, or...

03:23.454 --> 03:26.291
Here is the company review
I prepared.

03:26.750 --> 03:28.959
Lost a lot of sleep putting
this little baby together.

03:28.960 --> 03:32.379
But no rest
for the wicked, am I right?

03:41.056 --> 03:43.473
So get this.
After all that work,

03:43.474 --> 03:45.225
I didn't even get to go
to the meeting.

03:46.812 --> 03:49.355
I swear, Sweetie, sometimes...

03:50.148 --> 03:52.357
Yeah, I'm still sitting
with the assistants.

03:52.358 --> 03:54.735
But, all that changes tomorrow.

03:54.736 --> 03:56.154
When Bradley--

03:56.697 --> 04:00.700
Mr. Preston officially
takes over for his father.

04:01.660 --> 04:04.411
Yep. His father said,
right in front of him,

04:04.412 --> 04:06.997
that I was next in line for VP.

04:06.998 --> 04:09.585
So, he knows my value
to the company.

04:11.086 --> 04:13.503
And he's good-looking,
and he's single

04:13.504 --> 04:15.464
and charming,
and blah, blah, blah.

04:15.465 --> 04:18.050
And I told you how flirty he was
with me at the Christmas party.

04:18.051 --> 04:19.219
Whoo!

04:20.261 --> 04:21.096
But...

04:21.722 --> 04:23.681
That has nothing to do
with anything.

04:25.559 --> 04:27.060
We just need to focus on...

04:28.103 --> 04:31.022
the new office, the new title...

04:33.734 --> 04:35.443
...maybe that bigger apartment.

04:39.990 --> 04:41.783
We're gonna
spread our wings a little.

04:43.869 --> 04:45.120
It's not over for us.

04:46.663 --> 04:47.955
Best is yet to come.

04:50.250 --> 04:51.752
Well, exactly.

04:53.962 --> 04:55.213
We deserve it.

05:01.928 --> 05:03.179
You deserve it.

05:04.973 --> 05:06.099
Hmm?

05:10.103 --> 05:12.105
Up you go. Come on.

05:18.028 --> 05:19.112
Mmm.

05:22.699 --> 05:24.200
We deserve it.

05:26.036 --> 05:27.161
Mmm!

05:27.162 --> 05:28.747
It's time. Okay.

05:31.667 --> 05:33.668
Who'll have
what it takes to outwit...

05:33.669 --> 05:35.127
- Outplay, outlast.
- ...outplay, and outlast...

05:35.128 --> 05:36.378
all the rest.

05:36.379 --> 05:38.214
This is Survivor.

05:40.967 --> 05:43.929
If Kishan gets voted off
tonight, I swear to God.

05:46.347 --> 05:47.683
That's what I'm saying.

05:58.359 --> 06:00.320
Ladies and gentlemen, may
I have your attention please?

06:00.946 --> 06:04.700
I'd like to present to you your
new president, Bradley Preston.

06:09.454 --> 06:10.705
This is Marshall, IT...

06:10.706 --> 06:12.666
Marshall, look forward
to working with you.

06:12.999 --> 06:15.167
- Sonja. Sales.
- Nice to meet you, Mr. Preston.

06:15.168 --> 06:17.545
- Mmm.
- And finally, Sierra, Marketing.

06:17.546 --> 06:18.713
All right, sit down,
sit down, sit down.

06:18.714 --> 06:20.131
Okay, everybody back to work.

06:21.257 --> 06:22.800
Got a few things to talk to you
about in the office, okay?

06:22.801 --> 06:23.718
Sure.

06:23.719 --> 06:24.802
Soon as we can,
we gotta get you--

06:24.803 --> 06:26.555
- Mr. Preston!
- Hi!

06:27.013 --> 06:28.557
Call me Bradley.
Nice to meet you.

06:29.099 --> 06:30.766
Oh, um...

06:30.767 --> 06:34.479
Linda Liddle.
We spoke at the Christmas party.

06:34.980 --> 06:36.731
- Um...
- Oh. That's right.

06:36.732 --> 06:38.065
No, yes. Of course.

06:38.066 --> 06:39.524
Of course,
it's great to see you again.

06:39.525 --> 06:41.986
Yes. You, too. And I'm so sorry
about your father.

06:41.987 --> 06:44.739
- I appreciate that.
- He was a very admirable man.

06:44.740 --> 06:45.740
He really
took me under his wing.

06:45.741 --> 06:47.700
- Yes. Me, too.
- Um...

06:47.701 --> 06:51.621
But I am so excited about this
opportunity to help you execute

06:51.622 --> 06:53.623
...your strategic vision

06:53.624 --> 06:56.458
and lead this company
into a new era of, um...

06:56.459 --> 06:58.336
Um...

06:59.755 --> 07:00.756
Era of success.

07:01.923 --> 07:04.299
- Exactly.
- Well, I hope to do just that.

07:04.300 --> 07:05.217
It's gonna be
a lot of work though.

07:05.218 --> 07:06.637
Big shoes to fill, right?

07:07.470 --> 07:08.429
Gonna need
all the help I can get.

07:10.932 --> 07:13.893
Well, and I have
the right shoes already.

07:13.894 --> 07:15.186
What's that?

07:15.562 --> 07:18.480
I call these my Liddle Mules.

07:18.481 --> 07:21.233
Had these girls a long time.
A lot of miles on them.

07:21.234 --> 07:24.820
And they can carry any load
you throw their way.

07:24.821 --> 07:26.488
- Yeah. I gotta get to it.
- Okay.

07:26.489 --> 07:27.531
Okay.

07:27.532 --> 07:28.991
Oh, my gosh. Look at your shoes.

07:28.992 --> 07:31.828
Those are fancy-pants.

07:32.287 --> 07:34.705
Just don't step
in any puddles, right?

07:34.706 --> 07:36.249
I'm sorry, I didn't catch that.

07:37.083 --> 07:38.835
Don't step in any puddles.

07:40.170 --> 07:41.838
- I'll try to avoid that.
- Okay.

07:42.798 --> 07:45.133
All right. Get back to work.

07:47.052 --> 07:48.970
All right, gentlemen. Let's get
our P's and Q's in order.

07:49.429 --> 07:51.640
Barbara, lovely to see you.
Can you hold my calls?

07:54.267 --> 07:55.643
No, that went well.

07:55.644 --> 07:56.686
You just wanna go with

07:56.687 --> 07:58.980
the, uh, consulting firm's
recommendations?

08:00.190 --> 08:01.273
That's funny, right?

08:01.274 --> 08:03.483
A consulting firm
hiring a consulting firm.

08:03.484 --> 08:05.152
- What is that?
- What?

08:05.153 --> 08:06.071
This.

08:06.487 --> 08:07.614
I don't know.

08:08.406 --> 08:09.448
- Smell it.
- No.

08:09.449 --> 08:10.825
- Yes.
- No.

08:10.826 --> 08:11.910
Yes.

08:19.793 --> 08:20.836
Smell it.

08:26.507 --> 08:27.508
Tuna fish.

08:28.594 --> 08:29.720
Tuna fish.

08:32.180 --> 08:33.806
It's that disgusting woman.

08:33.807 --> 08:36.684
The one who accosted me
with Payless orthopedics.

08:36.685 --> 08:39.729
Linda Liddle. Your father
promised her a promotion.

08:39.730 --> 08:41.856
- From manager to vice president.
- Did he?

08:41.857 --> 08:43.817
A big bump in title and salary.

08:44.109 --> 08:45.275
- Yeah.
- She's been waiting for it.

08:45.276 --> 08:47.195
Right. Well.
Donovan's getting that job.

08:48.529 --> 08:51.323
Your father relied on Linda.
Real workhorse.

08:51.324 --> 08:52.825
I dump everything on her.

08:52.826 --> 08:54.243
Does it look like I give a shit?

08:54.244 --> 08:55.870
It doesn't, right?
'Cause I don't.

08:55.871 --> 08:58.414
My father's not here anymore.
It's Donovan's.

08:59.415 --> 09:01.333
Plus, I already told them.
And move her.

09:01.334 --> 09:02.710
Satellite office, maybe.

09:02.711 --> 09:05.756
Somewhere far.
She makes me sick.

09:07.924 --> 09:09.342
We have Bangkok coming up.

09:09.968 --> 09:12.386
And we haven't even
cracked Appendix-D.

09:12.387 --> 09:14.805
Donovan will drown on his own.

09:14.806 --> 09:16.265
The whole thing could fall apart
without her.

09:16.266 --> 09:17.934
Okay. Fine.

09:18.727 --> 09:19.728
Bring her.

09:20.311 --> 09:22.312
She'll get Don-O up to speed.
And then we'll ship her out.

09:31.489 --> 09:33.115
Wait, wait, wait,
this is funny...

09:35.076 --> 09:36.244
That little shake...

09:37.120 --> 09:38.955
Whoop.

09:41.207 --> 09:42.834
All right. Ah.

09:43.544 --> 09:45.837
Gotta get back to work.

09:47.380 --> 09:50.341
All right. Back to work.

09:51.009 --> 09:53.469
Well, they seem kind of chummy.

09:53.595 --> 09:56.139
Well, yeah, he's being promoted
to vice president.

09:57.223 --> 09:58.891
Sorry. I'm sorry, what?

09:58.892 --> 10:00.726
Yeah, I'm typing
the company-wide email

10:00.727 --> 10:01.895
about it right now.

10:02.187 --> 10:04.229
- Oh, tell me you're kidding.
- Mm-mm-mm.

10:04.230 --> 10:06.732
I literally looked
at his LinkedIn profile,

10:06.733 --> 10:09.151
and they were in
the same frat in college.

10:09.152 --> 10:11.946
And they play golf together.
So, duh.

10:31.967 --> 10:33.176
Linda, what the heck?

10:33.719 --> 10:36.345
Uh, my final question would be,
how above and beyond

10:36.346 --> 10:38.513
would you be willing
to go for me?

10:38.514 --> 10:40.432
Yes?

10:40.433 --> 10:41.726
Mr. Preston?

10:41.727 --> 10:42.644
I'm in a meeting.

10:42.978 --> 10:44.896
I'm sorry. I just need
a moment of your time.

10:45.689 --> 10:47.023
- Right, well, I'm--
- Please.

10:48.233 --> 10:49.234
Please.

10:49.651 --> 10:50.485
Sure.

10:50.986 --> 10:51.987
We'll be in touch.

10:53.113 --> 10:54.781
Thanks for coming in.

10:57.158 --> 10:58.159
Sorry.

11:00.161 --> 11:01.370
Sorry to barge in like this--

11:01.371 --> 11:03.914
Nope. Open door policy.
What's up?

11:03.915 --> 11:06.375
Uh-- Well, I just heard
about the job--

11:06.376 --> 11:08.211
You're unhappy about
not getting the promotion.

11:08.920 --> 11:09.920
Well, yes.

11:09.921 --> 11:11.214
Yeah. Okay.

11:11.757 --> 11:13.925
Yes, respectfully, uh...

11:14.843 --> 11:16.677
Donovan has been here
for six months,

11:16.678 --> 11:19.264
and I have been here
for seven years, and-and--

11:20.348 --> 11:21.516
I hear you.

11:21.892 --> 11:24.770
Let's talk it out.
Come in, close the door.

11:25.436 --> 11:26.730
Let's talk about it.

11:29.399 --> 11:30.483
Hmm?

11:34.320 --> 11:35.572
Please, sit.

11:42.162 --> 11:45.456
Now, I'm going to be frank
with you. If that's all right.

11:46.041 --> 11:48.418
I know that you are great
with numbers.

11:49.210 --> 11:51.003
Kind of a savant.

11:51.004 --> 11:52.462
- Right?
- I am good with numbers, yes.

11:52.463 --> 11:54.882
Yes, and I've carefully
reviewed a lot of that work,

11:54.883 --> 11:58.052
and it is impressive,
so that's the positive.

11:58.053 --> 11:59.261
Thank you.

11:59.262 --> 12:01.306
But, I...

12:02.223 --> 12:04.349
...don't see you as being
somebody who's ready

12:04.350 --> 12:06.978
for an executive position
quite yet.

12:11.232 --> 12:12.232
Why?

12:12.233 --> 12:14.443
I guess, as a VP,
I would need somebody

12:14.444 --> 12:16.780
who is more of a people person.

12:17.363 --> 12:21.785
You know, somebody by my side
who is well-liked.

12:22.243 --> 12:23.662
Who can charm a room.

12:24.037 --> 12:25.871
Who can make a deal.

12:25.872 --> 12:27.332
Somebody who golfs.

12:28.416 --> 12:29.542
Does that make sense?

12:30.669 --> 12:32.502
You're jo-- You're joking?

12:32.503 --> 12:34.088
No. Oh, uh...

12:34.089 --> 12:36.090
Right here. On your--

12:36.091 --> 12:38.134
Yeah, you just have a little.
Right there.

12:38.844 --> 12:40.095
You got it.

12:41.012 --> 12:42.513
See, that's kinda
what I'm talking about.

12:45.559 --> 12:48.895
Yeah. I just don't think
you got it.

12:49.771 --> 12:51.022
To be blunt.

12:53.399 --> 12:55.777
What I will say, though,
you coming in here?

12:56.612 --> 12:58.070
I wouldn't have expected that
out of you.

12:58.071 --> 12:59.239
That took some balls.

12:59.740 --> 13:00.574
Oh, yeah.

13:03.243 --> 13:04.786
You know, I got an idea.

13:06.287 --> 13:07.789
Yeah, I tell you
what I'm gonna do.

13:08.624 --> 13:12.252
You know we have the Bangkok
merger coming up, right?

13:13.503 --> 13:14.462
Yes.

13:15.046 --> 13:16.006
Right, so...

13:16.715 --> 13:18.008
I want you on that plane.

13:19.092 --> 13:21.719
We still got outstanding issues
with Appendix-D.

13:21.720 --> 13:24.973
You take a crack at that,
solve it. Prove me wrong.

13:26.850 --> 13:27.768
That sounds fair to me.

13:28.894 --> 13:29.770
- You'll--
- Great.

13:30.520 --> 13:31.647
I'm glad we had this talk.

13:35.734 --> 13:36.777
Boom.

13:37.736 --> 13:38.861
Oh, hello.

13:38.862 --> 13:40.529
- Hello.
- Hey, sexy. Wow.

13:40.530 --> 13:42.698
Am I disturbing anything?

13:42.699 --> 13:44.533
No, no, no, we're just
wrapping it up. Hi, baby.

13:44.534 --> 13:46.410
- My God, this dress.
- Thank you.

13:46.411 --> 13:47.828
Mmm.

13:47.829 --> 13:50.455
Uh, Linda,
this is my fiancée, Zuri.

13:50.456 --> 13:51.875
Lovely to meet you.

13:54.419 --> 13:55.754
Happy fiancée.

13:56.379 --> 13:59.006
Uh, yeah. I am. Thank you?

13:59.007 --> 14:01.383
Linda's one of
our best and brightest.

14:01.384 --> 14:02.552
Thanks for stopping in.

14:02.553 --> 14:04.136
- Nice to meet you.
- Yeah, sure.

14:04.137 --> 14:06.221
Oh, Linda, before you go.
Uh...

14:06.222 --> 14:09.685
Forgot to mention. I've received
a few complaints about you.

14:10.727 --> 14:12.311
- Complaints?
- Yes.

14:12.312 --> 14:15.189
Noxious odors,
I think was the term.

14:15.190 --> 14:18.359
Uh... Tuna fish? Does that
ring a bell? At the desk.

14:19.194 --> 14:22.197
Company policy. Just...
Lunch, it's for the breakroom.

14:23.031 --> 14:25.032
It's a workplace.
People are trying to focus.

14:25.033 --> 14:26.283
The odors,
they can be...

14:26.284 --> 14:27.786
- a distraction.
- Mm-hmm.

14:29.245 --> 14:30.246
You understand?

14:31.414 --> 14:32.415
Understood.

14:36.169 --> 14:38.170
- That was bad.
- Right?

14:47.639 --> 14:50.601
Don't cry. Don't cry.

14:51.392 --> 14:52.518
Don't.

14:58.942 --> 15:01.695
Linda.
You listen to me.

15:02.738 --> 15:03.947
You've got this.

15:09.953 --> 15:11.955
Because you are enough.

15:13.498 --> 15:15.041
Just the way you are.

15:19.796 --> 15:24.466
You are enough,
just the way you are.

15:29.765 --> 15:30.974
Oh, fuck me.

15:32.267 --> 15:35.937
Morning, gents!
Whoo-hee!

15:36.563 --> 15:37.397
Well...

15:38.106 --> 15:41.276
Who else is ready
and raring to fly high?

15:43.654 --> 15:45.780
I am.

15:45.781 --> 15:48.991
Mr. Preston. I was working
on Appendix-D last night.

15:48.992 --> 15:50.450
I think I may have found
a loophole

15:50.451 --> 15:52.037
that could fix
all of our problems.

15:52.788 --> 15:54.831
Love to bend your ear
once everyone's settled.

15:55.624 --> 15:56.624
What?

15:56.625 --> 15:59.459
Let's go, boys.
Cocks in the air.

15:59.460 --> 16:00.921
Relax, Linda.

16:02.088 --> 16:03.715
You work too hard.

16:18.313 --> 16:20.230
Wait till you guys see
Siam Country Golf Club.

16:20.231 --> 16:21.732
That eighteenth hole.

16:21.733 --> 16:24.526
Straight uphill. Dogleg left.
I know my boy's gonna love it.

16:24.527 --> 16:27.781
I gotta show you something...

16:28.406 --> 16:30.032
...you are gonna love.

16:30.033 --> 16:31.827
Check this out.

16:43.046 --> 16:44.590
What the hell is this?

16:47.593 --> 16:49.844
- What the fuck?
- I'm Linda Liddle.

16:51.512 --> 16:53.222
No fucking way.

16:53.223 --> 16:55.515
- I wanna be the next...
- That's her?

16:55.516 --> 16:58.102
- ...Survivor!
- Oh, my God.

17:00.105 --> 17:02.232
Shh.

17:02.941 --> 17:04.109
I love to read.

17:04.860 --> 17:07.194
But I'm crazy
about the outdoors, too!

17:11.241 --> 17:13.450
I can do bushcraft
with my eyes closed.

17:17.122 --> 17:18.205
You can make fire

17:18.206 --> 17:19.456
- three different ways.
- No fucking way.

17:19.457 --> 17:21.250
And I know all three of them.

17:26.965 --> 17:28.841
LINDA
I work in Strategy and Planning,

17:28.842 --> 17:32.386
so you know I'll always be
